card.statement:
The homomorphism $\Phi$ defines a representation of $\widehat{\mathfrak{sl}}_2$ on the spaces $N_{S}$, $N_{i,S}$, $M_S$, and $M_{i,S}$. We also have the following vector space isomorphisms

\begin{equation*}
M_{S}\simeq
y_{k_1}^{-1}\ldots y_{k_n}^{-1}\mathbb C[{\bf x},{\bf y}_{S}^{-1},\widehat{\bf y}_{S}], \;
M_{i,S}\simeq x_i^{-1}y_{k_1}^{-1}\ldots y_{k_n}^{-1}\mathbb C[x_i^{-1},{\bf y}_{S}^{-1},\widehat{{\bf x_i}},\widehat{\bf y}_{S}].
\end{equation*}
